{
  "_comment": "Shared by backend/tests/test_authorship.py, src/lib/authorship.test.ts and apple/LunaschalCore TextAuthorshipTests. Authors: u typed, s speech-to-text, a AI. A span may carry a third element, the recording it came from. Lengths are Unicode code points. `runs` is how every client slices text by spans; `merges` is the server's change rule (backend/authorship.py merge_edit). `aligned` is how the clients colour Markdown: the rendered pieces, in source order, each get the authors of the source characters they came from (AuthorAligner / alignAuthors).",
